# Line endings are a property of THIS REPOSITORY, not of whoever checked it out.
#
# Before this file the repo carried 1,091 LF, 252 CRLF and 14 MIXED-ending
# files, because `core.autocrlf` is per-machine (it was `false` here) and every
# editor and script wrote whatever it liked. Mixed files are the expensive ones:
# a normal edit rewrites the whole file's endings, so a six-line change lands as
# a 500-line diff and the real change becomes unreviewable. Worse, the usual
# repair tools cause it — `sed -i` under MSYS, Python's `write_text`, and
# editors that normalise on save all convert a whole mixed file silently.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes git normalise to LF in the index on add and check out
# LF on every platform, so the state above cannot recur regardless of local
# config. Windows tooling reads LF fine; nothing here needs CRLF.
#
# The repo was renormalised in one commit alongside this file, verified by
# `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` coming back empty against the previous tree —
# i.e. endings changed and content did not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types, declared explicitly rather than left to content sniffing: a
# false "text" verdict on any of these would corrupt the file on checkout.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.mcpack  binary
*.mcaddon binary
*.io      binary
*.lxf     binary
